(d) As provided in this article, no vehicle shall stop, stand, or park, except momentarily to pick up or discharge a passenger or passengers:
(1) In front of a public or private driveway;
(2) Within fifteen (15) feet of a fire hydrant;
(3) Within twenty (20) feet of a crosswalk at an intersection;
(4) Within thirty (30) feet upon the approach to any flashing signal, stop sign, yield sign, or traffic-control signal located at the side of a roadway;
(5) Within twenty (20) feet of the driveway entrance to any fire station or on the side of a street opposite the entrance to any fire station within seventy-five (75) feet of such entrance; or
(6) At any place where official signs prohibit standing.
(e) The provisions of this section shall apply to residentially zoned (R-1, R-2, R-43, R-4 and R-5), neighborhood commercial zoned (C-1), and planned use development zoned (PUD) areas.
